The  utility adds a user to the system, creating and populating a
home directory if necessary.  Any skeleton files will be provided
for the new user if they exist in the directory (see the option).
Default values for the base directory, the time of  password  ex‐
piry, the time of account expiry, primary group, the skeleton di‐
rectory,  the range from which the uid will be allocated, and de‐
fault login shell can be provided in the file, which, if  running
as  root,  is  created using the built‐in defaults if it does not
exist.  The first form of the command shown above (using the  op‐
